      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The options",
      "heading": "COSHH software that reads the safety data sheet",
      "html": "<p>I make Quickler, so read this with that in mind. Every line about another tool comes from its own website, checked on 18 November 2026. Where I could not check something, I leave it out.</p><ul><li><strong>COSHH.app</strong> (<a href=\"https://coshh.app/coshh-risk-assessment-software\" rel=\"noopener\">coshh.app</a>). Photograph the product label; it finds the safety data sheet and drafts a COSHH report. Free plan with 5 scans; Starter £7.99 a month for 25 scans. <em>Better when:</em> you have many products, little time and want a low monthly price.</li><li><strong>OpSemble</strong> (<a href=\"https://opsemble.co.uk/features/coshh-assessment-software.html\" rel=\"noopener\">opsemble.co.uk</a>). Upload the supplier's safety data sheet and the hazards, PPE and first aid are pulled out for you to check, into a chemical register. £9 per user a month on top of a £29 a month platform fee. <em>Better when:</em> you want a COSHH register as part of a small-business safety system.</li><li><strong>Paddl</strong> (<a href=\"https://paddl-ai.co/insights/safety-data-sheet-to-coshh-risk-assessment\" rel=\"noopener\">paddl-ai.co</a>). Reads an uploaded safety data sheet and builds the COSHH record: hazards, signal word, PPE, first aid, handling and storage. £69 per location a month, 30-day free trial. Its guides are written for food and hospitality businesses. <em>Better when:</em> you run kitchens or venues and want COSHH next to food safety records.</li><li><strong>Quickler</strong> (<a href=\"/pages/how-it-works.html\">how it works</a>). Send the safety data sheet in WhatsApp, then say what the product is used for, by whom, how often and where. Quickler fills your firm's own COSHH form in Word or PDF. You check and sign it. <em>Better when:</em> you are a consultant or H&amp;S team with your own COSHH form, and the time goes on retyping sheets into it.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
