      "heading": "What only the person on the job can add",
      "html": "<p>The sheet knows the product, not your task. COSHH regulation 6 asks the assessment to consider the level, type and duration of exposure, and the circumstances of the work. Someone who knows the job still has to say how much is used, how often, where, who else is near and what controls are really there. Quickler asks those questions in WhatsApp, so the gaps are filled on site, not guessed at a desk.</p><p>Graeme Clark, an H&amp;S consultant at Ethos Safety, went from 1 to 2 hours of write-up per report to 14 minutes on average. The walk takes as long as it takes. The typing afterwards is what goes. £75 a month per phone number, or £750 a year. 14-day free trial, no card needed. <a href=\"/pages/demo.html\">See a real Record</a>.</p>"
